                <pb facs="0642" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-01T09:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                                1925—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:25
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Yesterday the Premier in conversation with the American Administrator General
                    declared unequivocally that the Government, in which he said his position was
                    for the future quite secure, has no thought of allowing agreements with American
                    advisers to lapse at their expiration on September 30. He gave expression of
                    regard for Administrator General himself and hoped he would continue as chief of
                    the staff of American officials. Millspaugh contemplates journey to America
                    later in year to employ other assistants.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
